Feature: Therapeutic Area Study Aggregation and Analysis

  This feature aggregates study data by therapeutic area, providing insights into study counts, completion status, ongoing status, and average enrolled subjects. The results are displayed in the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results" with columns: therapeutic_area, total_studies, completed_studies, ongoing_studies, avg_enrolled_subjects.

  Background:
    Given the authoritative source for study status and subject counts is "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis"
    And the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" contains columns: therapeutic_area, study_title, study_conduct_status, enrolled_subjects_qty
    And the output table is "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results" with columns: therapeutic_area, total_studies, completed_studies, ongoing_studies, avg_enrolled_subjects
    And only records with non-null therapeutic_area are included
    And therapeutic_area values are used as-is (no mapping/normalization required)
    And all records are considered (no date range filter)
    And duplicate "total_studies" column in output is removed (only one total_studies column)
    And null enrolled_subjects_qty values are excluded from avg_enrolled_subjects calculation

  Scenario: Aggregate study data by therapeutic area (happy path)
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" contains valid data for therapeutic_area, study_conduct_status, enrolled_subjects_qty
    When the data is grouped by therapeutic_area
    Then total_studies is calculated as the count of all studies per therapeutic_area
    And completed_studies is calculated as the count of studies where study_conduct_status = "Completed" per therapeutic_area
    And ongoing_studies is calculated as the count of studies where study_conduct_status = "Ongoing" per therapeutic_area
    And avg_enrolled_subjects is calculated as the average of enrolled_subjects_qty per therapeutic_area, excluding nulls
    And the results are written to "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results" with columns: therapeutic_area, total_studies, completed_studies, ongoing_studies, avg_enrolled_subjects

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven aggregation for multiple therapeutic areas
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" contains studies for <therapeutic_area>
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the output for <therapeutic_area> should be:
      | therapeutic_area | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
      | <therapeutic_area> | <total_studies> | <completed_studies> | <ongoing_studies> | <avg_enrolled_subjects> |

    Examples:
      | therapeutic_area | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
      | Oncology         | 10            | 6                 | 4               | 120.5                 |
      | Cardiology       | 8             | 3                 | 5               | 98.0                  |
      | Neurology        | 5             | 2                 | 3               | 75.2                  |

  Scenario: Handle null or missing values in key columns
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" contains records with null therapeutic_area
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then records with null therapeutic_area are excluded from the results

    Given the table contains records with null enrolled_subjects_qty
    When calculating avg_enrolled_subjects
    Then null enrolled_subjects_qty values are excluded from the average calculation

    Given the table contains records with null study_conduct_status
    When calculating completed_studies and ongoing_studies
    Then records with null study_conduct_status are not counted in completed_studies or ongoing_studies

  Scenario: Error handling for invalid study_conduct_status values
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" contains records with study_conduct_status not in ["Completed", "Ongoing"]
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then such records are counted in total_studies but not in completed_studies or ongoing_studies

  Scenario: Error handling for missing output table
    Given the output table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results" does not exist
    When the aggregation logic attempts to write results
    Then an error is raised with message "Output table purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results does not exist"

  Scenario: Validation of output data types and formats
    Given the aggregation logic has completed
    When the results are written to "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results"
    Then therapeutic_area is a non-null string
    And total_studies, completed_studies, ongoing_studies are non-negative integers
    And avg_enrolled_subjects is a double with up to 2 decimal places

  Scenario: Exclusion of irrelevant study types or products
    Given there are no specified filters or exclusions for study types, statuses, or products
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then all studies in "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" are included in the aggregation

  Scenario: Output display requirements
    Given the aggregation logic has completed
    When the results are available
    Then the results are displayed in the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results" with columns: therapeutic_area, total_studies, completed_studies, ongoing_studies, avg_enrolled_subjects

  Scenario: Calculation rules for aggregation
    Given the following calculation rules:
      | Field                | Rule                                                                 |
      | total_studies        | COUNT(*) per therapeutic_area                                        |
      | completed_studies    | COUNT(*) where study_conduct_status = "Completed" per therapeutic_area|
      | ongoing_studies      | COUNT(*) where study_conduct_status = "Ongoing" per therapeutic_area |
      | avg_enrolled_subjects| AVG(enrolled_subjects_qty) per therapeutic_area, excluding nulls     |
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the output values follow these rules

  Scenario: Data integrity validation
    Given the aggregation logic has completed
    When the results are written
    Then for each therapeutic_area, total_studies >= completed_studies + ongoing_studies
    And completed_studies and ongoing_studies are mutually exclusive per study

  Scenario: Error scenario for all null enrolled_subjects_qty
    Given all enrolled_subjects_qty values for a therapeutic_area are null
    When calculating avg_enrolled_subjects
    Then avg_enrolled_subjects is set to null for that therapeutic_area

  Scenario: Error scenario for all null study_conduct_status
    Given all study_conduct_status values for a therapeutic_area are null
    When calculating completed_studies and ongoing_studies
    Then completed_studies and ongoing_studies are set to 0 for that therapeutic_area

  Scenario: Data-driven test for null and non-null enrolled_subjects_qty
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" contains the following data:
      | therapeutic_area | study_conduct_status | enrolled_subjects_qty |
      | Oncology         | Completed            | 100                   |
      | Oncology         | Ongoing              | null                  |
      | Oncology         | Completed            | 150                   |
      | Oncology         | Ongoing              | 120                   |
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the output for Oncology should be:
      | therapeutic_area | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
      | Oncology         | 4             | 2                 | 2               | 123.33                |

  Scenario: Data-driven test for invalid study_conduct_status values
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" contains the following data:
      | therapeutic_area | study_conduct_status | enrolled_subjects_qty |
      | Cardiology       | Completed            | 80                    |
      | Cardiology       | Ongoing              | 100                   |
      | Cardiology       | Terminated           | 90                    |
      | Cardiology       | null                 | 110                   |
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the output for Cardiology should be:
      | therapeutic_area | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
      | Cardiology       | 4             | 1                 | 1               | 95.0                  |
